[agent:bash] cat data/task.md; echo "---HEAD HISTORY---"; head -3 data/airquality_history.csv; echo "---HEAD FORECAST---"; head -3 data/forecast_days.csv; echo "---COUNTS---"; wc -l data/*.csv
[agent:result] # Capstone — air-quality PM2.5 forecasting (regression)
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] `data/airquality_history.csv` is a daily history (`date, pm25_lag1, temperature, humidity, wind_speed, pressure, precipitation, pm25`) where `pm25` is the measured air quality and `pm25_lag1` is the previous day's value. `data/forecast_days.csv` holds later days WITHOUT `pm25` — predict it for each.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Build the full pipeline on the platform:
[agent:result] 1. Engineer features (weather + lag/rolling air-quality signals) into a feature group `airqeda516`.
[agent:result] 2. Assemble a training dataset `airqtdeda516`.
[agent:result] 3. Train a PM2.5 regressor and register it as `airqmodeleda516` WITH its evaluation metrics.
[agent:result] 4. Predict every row of `forecast_days.csv` into a feature table `airqprededa516` (record key `date`, column `pm25_pred`).
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Target: RMSE ≤ 2.202 µg/m³ on the held-out days (train-mean baseline ≈ 2.601).
